  "tuning": "Fix round 1 (Nov 12): the r4 sets folded yellow and green into one amber band (97 % of chroma pixels in one 30-degree band) and read as a sepia filter beside 1-TR (judge). Re-tuned on the HDR dump of the look places (no hour EV, W0 keys): the amber band rotated -3 deg toward orange (a* x1.12 in the mids) and kept at chroma x0.98, the olive band only -6 deg, greens untouched, Orchil violets x1.55 so Brea's violet is the most saturated hue (dump: violet max 46.8 vs grass p90 42.0 field, 45.2 vs 41.6 aim, 47.3 vs 39.8 close); shadows shifted toward rose in L*a*b* by (5.5, -5) at chroma x0.85 (the full-resolution frames, with GTAO, put the darkest fifth at a* 8-10: a larger b* shift turned them blue-violet); mid b* x0.82; highlights x0.42 chroma; a tone curve on L* that opens the top (60 -> 68.5, 72 -> 82) so p99 does not fall below the W0 output (field 73.7 vs W0 73.4). Bars met on the dump: 22/40 against r4 14/40; the rest (p99 >= 88, clip, spread, hi10 chroma) need the sun, the sky and the sea (world-sky L-03/L-04/L-06, world-ground).",
